Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `consume` takes `p`, but `p` is used again later
  --> tests/ui/struct_use_after_move.jet:11:13
    |
 11 |     consume(p)
    |             ^
  --> tests/ui/struct_use_after_move.jet:12:13
    |
 12 |     print(p.x)
    |             ^ `p` is used again here
 Why: `consume` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `p` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `p.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `p`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `p`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209
